=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
Live diagnostics on all relevant devices confirm that PC15 (172.18.51.15/24) and PC16 (172.18.51.16/24) have full, healthy bidirectional connectivity. Both hosts are assigned addresses in the same /24 subnet with gateway 172.18.51.254, both are wired into switch10 (eth1 and eth2 respectively), and switch10 itself is a flat untagged VLAN-1 bridge with all ports in forwarding state. No port isolation flag is set on either port (verified via `ip -d link show`). There are no iptables rules on either endpoint, no ebtables rules on switch10 or mswitch2, and no tc traffic-shaping policies. The upstream mswitch2 correctly places switch10's uplink (eth2) in the br_vlan51 bridge domain, consistent with the 172.18.51.x addressing. Ping tests — standard 84-byte and large 1428-byte frames — complete in both directions with 0% packet loss. ARP tables are correctly populated on both hosts. Every layer from L2 MAC learning through L3 IP forwarding is functioning normally. The fault described in the helpdesk ticket (total bidirectional blackout between PC15 and PC16) does not exist in the current lab state. This appears to be a false alarm or a transient condition that has since resolved; no corrective action is required.
=== END ===